{"parentUuid":"46780f69-ab5f-41a1-9f19-86564bf13e89","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d59525ad-07c1-4649-bb80-18ba1c402e6b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MBmZoZVXVwpdVjBYVqeweJ","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PostToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"Agent\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code post-task'\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"TaskCreate|TaskUpdate\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code post-todo'\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"PreToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"Agent\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code pre-task'\"\n          }\n==> hackathon.md <==\n# neatHack build log: Kedge\n\n## Project\n**Kedge** is a supervisor that pulls unattended coding agents back on course. It turns failing dependency-bump PRs green, catches silent drift (deleted or skipped tests, edits outside the plan, loops, budget overruns, false success claims), rolls back to the last good commit, and retries.\n\n\n==> docs/submission-checklist.md <==\n# Submission checklist\n\nMaps each item judges check ([neatlogs.com/hackathon](https://neatlogs.com/hackathon)) to the evidence that proves it. `PENDING` means something is still missing.\n\nSubmit on X by quoting the official neatlogs post with the team, name, project, public repo and demo. Submissions open Mon Oct 12, 7:00 PM IST; our planned close is 11:55 PM IST (the Discord cutoff is authoritative).\n\n==> docs/plans/2026-10-10-kedge.md <==\n# Kedge Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Build a CLI supervisor that runs headless Claude Code to turn failing dependency PRs green. After every step it detects silent drift, rolls back to the last good commit, and retries.\nREADME.md:28:| Judging items mapped to proof | [docs/submission-checklist.md](docs/submission-checklist.md) |\nREADME.md:65:Build log: [hackathon.md](hackathon.md). Design and plan: [design](docs/designs/kedge-design.md) · [spec](docs/specs/kedge-spec.md) · [plan](docs/plans/2026-10-10-kedge.md).\ndocs/README.md:8:| Check our claims (judges) | [Evidence](evidence.md) · [Submission checklist](submission-checklist.md) |\ndocs/README.md:42:- Visual design of the dashboard: [PRODUCT.md](../PRODUCT.md), [DESIGN.md](../DESIGN.md)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c1845b53-5bce-4882-a528-f71e711eaa72","timestamp":"2026-10-12T13:53:22.538Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PostToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"Agent\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code post-task'\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"TaskCreate|TaskUpdate\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code post-todo'\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"PreToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"Agent\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code pre-task'\"\n          }\n==> hackathon.md <==\n# neatHack build log: Kedge\n\n## Project\n**Kedge** is a supervisor that pulls unattended coding agents back on course. It turns failing dependency-bump PRs green, catches silent drift (deleted or skipped tests, edits outside the plan, loops, budget overruns, false success claims), rolls back to the last good commit, and retries.\n\n\n==> docs/submission-checklist.md <==\n# Submission checklist\n\nMaps each item judges check ([neatlogs.com/hackathon](https://neatlogs.com/hackathon)) to the evidence that proves it. `PENDING` means something is still missing.\n\nSubmit on X by quoting the official neatlogs post with the team, name, project, public repo and demo. Submissions open Mon Oct 12, 7:00 PM IST; our planned close is 11:55 PM IST (the Discord cutoff is authoritative).\n\n==> docs/plans/2026-10-10-kedge.md <==\n# Kedge Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Build a CLI supervisor that runs headless Claude Code to turn failing dependency PRs green. After every step it detects silent drift, rolls back to the last good commit, and retries.\nREADME.md:28:| Judging items mapped to proof | [docs/submission-checklist.md](docs/submission-checklist.md) |\nREADME.md:65:Build log: [hackathon.md](hackathon.md). Design and plan: [design](docs/designs/kedge-design.md) · [spec](docs/specs/kedge-spec.md) · [plan](docs/plans/2026-10-10-kedge.md).\ndocs/README.md:8:| Check our claims (judges) | [Evidence](evidence.md) · [Submission checklist](submission-checklist.md) |\ndocs/README.md:42:- Visual design of the dashboard: [PRODUCT.md](../PRODUCT.md), [DESIGN.md](../DESIGN.md)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"46780f69-ab5f-41a1-9f19-