{"parentUuid":"cb3562fc-5d39-4a57-99c4-c29368761d4e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxTL9qT9RcmUsQnUtAkk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'd remove 27 of the 172 tracked files. Removing a file from the repo leaves it in the git history and keeps your local copy, but I'll only do it once you OK the list.\n\n**Remove (27 files):**\n1. `.impeccable/` (15 files): the design tool's working state, its review screenshots and its question logs. No code or docs use them.\n2. `diagrams/` at the repo root (10 files): the LinkedIn and tweet images, the first-PR card, and an older version of the loop diagram. The diagrams the docs use live in `docs/diagrams/`.\n3. `.claude/launch.json`: my local dev-server config.\n4. `.claude/skills/neathack/SKILL.md`: our private hackathon helper skill.\n\nI'll also delete the links to these files from [PRODUCT.md](PRODUCT.md) and [docs/README.md](docs/README.md), so no link is broken.\n\n**Optional:** `docs/plans/2026-10-10-kedge.md`, our hour-by-hour build plan split between Farouk and Haikeys. It's internal, but it shows how we built the project, and the README links to it. I'd keep it.\n\n**Keep:**\n- **The product:** all code, tests, `pricing.json`, `targets.json`, `.env.example`, `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock`.\n- **Proof for the judges:** `docs/`, including the evidence, the business plan and the checklist that maps each judging point to its proof; `hackathon.md`, the build log that has the first Entire checkpoint as proof.\n- **Entire:** `.entire/` and `.claude/settings.json`. The latter holds the Entire hooks, which shows how we used Entire.\n- **Presentation:** `site/` (the dashboard) and `videos/` (the source for the film).\n- **Design:** `DESIGN.md` and `PRODUCT.md`. The film's colour tokens point to `DESIGN.md`.\n\nShould I go ahead with removing the 27 files, keeping the plan?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1892,"cache_read_input_tokens":307045,"output_tokens":1028,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":360},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1892,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1028,"cache_read_input_tokens":307045,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1892,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1892},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfxTL9W7cHE9tT6LbCasf","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"22e524b9-1959-49f5-8062-b338fdf76c0b","timestamp":"2026-10-12T13:53:34.369Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zorak/Documents/kedge","sessionId":"cd9da397-cf5a-4398-8a9d-d5ceb647cbb1","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"snoopy-knitting-penguin"}
